---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="Part 1: a small cache with a size limit serves a fixed stream of 200 requests, and you pick how it chooses what to evict. Part 2: a hot key expires and you watch the database load with and without request coalescing.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>. With <b>Request pattern</b> on "Popular items", <b>Eviction policy</b> on LRU and <b>Cache size</b> at 8, the cache gets 104 hits in 200 requests (52.0%). Switch <b>Eviction policy</b> to LFU: 117 hits (58.5%). Switch to FIFO: 93 hits (46.5%).</li>
    <li>Set <b>Request pattern</b> to "One-off scan mixed in": every second request is a key never seen again. LRU drops to 58 hits (29.0%), FIFO to 47 (23.5%), and LFU holds up at 92 (46.0%), because the keys it keeps have been asked for many times.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Request pattern</b> to "Favourites change halfway" and <b>Eviction policy</b> to LFU: 108 hits (54.0%), while LRU gets 164 (82.0%). LFU keeps the old favourites because of their high counts, so the new ones struggle to stay.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, then set <b>Cache size</b> to 4: LRU gets 63 hits (31.5%). Set it to 12: 128 hits (64.0%). Size often matters more than policy.</li>
    <li>In the stampede part, press <b>Reset stampede</b>. A hot key read 600 times a second expires and takes 2 seconds to rebuild. With <b>Coalesce requests</b> off, 1,200 queries hit the database and the peak is 700 queries per second against a capacity of 500: overloaded.</li>
    <li>Tick <b>Coalesce requests</b>: only 1 query is sent for the key, and the peak falls to 101 per second. Untick <b>Hot key expires</b> and the peak is the background 100.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset stampede</b>, then set <b>Requests per second for the hot key</b> to 300: the peak is 400, within capacity. Now set <b>Rebuild time</b> to 5 seconds: the peak is still 400, but it lasts 5 seconds and 1,500 queries are sent.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg ce" data-ce>
    <h3 class="ce-h">Part 1: which entry leaves a full cache?</h3>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Request pattern
        <select class="pg-in" data-pattern>
          <option value="popular" selected>Popular items</option>
          <option value="scan">One-off scan mixed in</option>
          <option value="shift">Favourites change halfway</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>Eviction policy
        <select class="pg-in" data-policy>
          <option value="lru" selected>LRU (least recently used)</option>
          <option value="lfu">LFU (least frequently used)</option>
          <option value="fifo">FIFO (first in, first out)</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>Cache size <input class="pg-in" type="range" min="2" max="20" step="1" value="8" data-size /> <b data-sizeval>8</b> entries</label>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note" data-patnote></p>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h4>Hit rate</h4><span class="pg-mono" data-rate></span><span class="pg-note" data-ratenote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-4)"><h4>Database reads</h4><span class="pg-mono" data-reads></span><span class="pg-note">one per miss</span></div>
    </div>
    <table class="ce-table">
      <caption class="pg-note">The same stream and size under each policy</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Policy</th><th scope="col">Hits</th><th scope="col">Hit rate</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody data-table></tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="pg-mono ce-strip" data-strip></p>
    <p class="pg-note" data-final></p>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>

    <h3 class="ce-h">Part 2: the hot key expires</h3>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Requests per second for the hot key <input class="pg-in" type="range" min="100" max="1000" step="100" value="600" data-sr /> <b data-srval>600</b></label>
      <label>Rebuild time <input class="pg-in" type="range" min="1" max="5" step="1" value="2" data-sb /> <b data-sbval>2</b> s</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label class="ce-check"><input type="checkbox" checked data-sx /> Hot key expires</label>
      <label class="ce-check"><input type="checkbox" data-sc /> Coalesce requests</label>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-sreset>Reset stampede</button>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-peakbox style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h4>Peak database load</h4><span class="pg-mono" data-peak></span><span class="pg-note" data-peaknote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-2)"><h4>Queries sent for the hot key</h4><span class="pg-mono" data-extra></span><span class="pg-note" data-extranote></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ce-chart" role="img" data-chart>
      <div class="ce-cap" data-cap><span>capacity</span></div>
      <div class="ce-cols" data-cols></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note">Queries per second for each of 10 seconds. The dashed line is what the database can serve.</p>
    <p class="pg-out" data-sverdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model for part 1: a fixed stream of 200 requests from one seed. Each miss reads the database and puts the key in the cache; when the cache is full one entry leaves first. LRU removes the entry used longest ago, LFU removes the one with the fewest requests since it entered (ties go to the least recently used), FIFO removes the one that entered first. "Popular items" draws from 30 keys where the key of rank n is asked in proportion to 1/n. "One-off scan" alternates 6 hot keys with keys that never come back. "Favourites change" uses 10 popular keys for 100 requests, then 10 different ones. Model for part 2: the key expires at the start of second 3. Every request that arrives before the rebuild finishes misses; without coalescing each one queries the database, with coalescing only the first does and the rest wait for its answer. The rest of the site adds a steady 100 queries per second, and the database can serve 500. Real databases slow down when overloaded, so a real rebuild gets longer and the spike worse. Small seeded streams show the shape of each effect, not the exact numbers a real workload would give.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, mulberry32 } from '../playground';
  type Policy = 'lru' | 'lfu' | 'fifo';
  type Pattern = 'popular' | 'scan' | 'shift';
  interface Entry { freq: number; last: number; born: number }

  const REQUESTS = 200; const SEED = 7; const STRIP = 60; const GROUP = 10;
  const POPULAR_KEYS = 30; const HOT_KEYS = 6; const SHIFT_KEYS = 10; const NEVER_AGAIN = 100;
  const PATTERNS: Record<Pattern, string> = {
    popular: 'A few keys are asked for far more often than the rest (30 keys, the busiest gets about one request in four).',
    scan: 'Every second request is for one of 6 busy keys; the others are keys that are asked for once and never again.',
    shift: 'The first 100 requests favour 10 keys; the last 100 favour 10 different keys.',
  };
  const POLICY_NAMES: Record<Policy, string> = { lru: 'LRU', lfu: 'LFU', fifo: 'FIFO' };
  const DEFAULTS = { pattern: 'popular', policy: 'lru', size: '8' };
  const S_DEFAULTS = { rate: '600', build: '2', expires: true, coalesce: false };
  const SECONDS = 10; const EXPIRY_SECOND = 3; const BASE_LOAD = 100; const DB_CAPACITY = 500;

  // Key of rank n (1 is busiest) is drawn in proportion to 1/n.
  function zipf(rand: () => number, n: number, offset: number) {
    let total = 0; for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) total += 1 / i;
    let x = rand() * total;
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) { x -= 1 / i; if (x <= 0) return offset + i - 1; }
    return offset + n - 1;
  }
  function makeStream(kind: Pattern): number[] {
    const r = mulberry32(SEED); const out: number[] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < REQUESTS; i++) {
      if (kind === 'popular') out.push(zipf(r, POPULAR_KEYS, 0));
      else if (kind === 'scan') out.push(i % 2 === 0 ? Math.floor(r() * HOT_KEYS) : NEVER_AGAIN + i);
      else out.push(i < REQUESTS / 2 ? zipf(r, SHIFT_KEYS, 0) : zipf(r, SHIFT_KEYS, SHIFT_KEYS));
    }
    return out;
  }
  function simulate(stream: number[], policy: Policy, size: number) {
    const cache = new Map<number, Entry>(); let hits = 0; const marks: boolean[] = []; let t = 0;
    for (const key of stream) {
      t++;
      const e = cache.get(key);
      if (e) { hits++; e.freq++; e.last = t; marks.push(true); continue; }
      marks.push(false);
      if (cache.size >= size) {
        let victim = -1; let best: number[] | null = null;
        for (const [k, v] of cache) {
          const score = policy === 'lru' ? [v.last] : policy === 'fifo' ? [v.born] : [v.freq, v.last];
          if (best === null || score[0] < best[0] || (score[0] === best[0] && score.length > 1 && score[1] < best[1])) { best = score; victim = k; }
        }
        cache.delete(victim);
      }
      cache.set(key, { freq: 1, last: t, born: t });
    }
    return { hits, marks, keys: [...cache.keys()].sort((a, b) => a - b) };
  }
  function stampede(rate: number, build: number, expires: boolean, coalesce: boolean) {
    const per: number[] = []; let extra = 0;
    for (let s = 0; s < SECONDS; s++) {
      let e = 0;
      if (expires) e = coalesce ? (s === EXPIRY_SECOND ? 1 : 0) : (s >= EXPIRY_SECOND && s < EXPIRY_SECOND + build ? rate : 0);
      extra += e; per.push(BASE_LOAD + e);
    }
    return { per, extra, peak: Math.max(...per) };
  }

  const fmt = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
  const pct = (n: number) => `${((100 * n) / REQUESTS).toFixed(1)}%`;
  const streams = new Map<Pattern, number[]>();

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ce]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    let frame = 0;
    function draw() {
      frame = 0;
      const pattern = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-pattern]').value as Pattern;
      const policy = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-policy]').value as Policy;
      const size = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-size]').value);
      let stream = streams.get(pattern); if (!stream) { stream = makeStream(pattern); streams.set(pattern, stream); }
      q('[data-sizeval]').textContent = String(size);
      q('[data-patnote]').textContent = PATTERNS[pattern];
      const results = (['lru', 'lfu', 'fifo'] as Policy[]).map((p) => ({ p, ...simulate(stream!, p, size) }));
      const mine = results.find((r) => r.p === policy)!;
      q('[data-rate]').textContent = pct(mine.hits);
      q('[data-ratenote]').textContent = `${fmt(mine.hits)} hits in ${fmt(REQUESTS)} requests`;
      q('[data-reads]').textContent = fmt(REQUESTS - mine.hits);
      const body = q('[data-table]'); body.textContent = '';
      for (const r of results) {
        const tr = document.createElement('tr'); if (r.p === policy) tr.className = 'sel';
        const th = document.createElement('th'); th.scope = 'row'; th.textContent = POLICY_NAMES[r.p] + (r.p === policy ? ' (selected)' : '');
        const a = document.createElement('td'); a.textContent = fmt(r.hits);
        const b = document.createElement('td'); b.textContent = pct(r.hits);
        tr.append(th, a, b); body.append(tr);
      }
      const letters = mine.marks.slice(0, STRIP).map((h) => (h ? 'H' : 'M'));
      const groups: string[] = []; for (let i = 0; i < letters.length; i += GROUP) groups.push(letters.slice(i, i + GROUP).join(''));
      q('[data-strip]').textContent = `First ${STRIP} requests (H hit, M miss): ${groups.join(' ')}`;
      q('[data-final]').textContent = `Keys in the cache at the end: ${mine.keys.map((k) => (k >= NEVER_AGAIN ? `one-off ${k}` : `k${k}`)).join(', ')}.`;
      const best = results.reduce((a, b) => (b.hits > a.hits ? b : a));
      const tie = results.filter((r) => r.hits === best.hits).length > 1;
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = `${POLICY_NAMES[policy]}: ${pct(mine.hits)} hit rate (${fmt(mine.hits)} of ${fmt(REQUESTS)}), with ${size} entries. ` +
        (tie ? 'Two or more policies tie for best on this stream.' : best.p === policy ? 'It is the best of the three on this stream.' : `${POLICY_NAMES[best.p]} does best here with ${pct(best.hits)}.`);

      // Part 2
      const rate = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-sr]').value); const build = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-sb]').value);
      const expires = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-sx]').checked; const coalesce = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-sc]').checked;
      q('[data-srval]').textContent = fmt(rate); q('[data-sbval]').textContent = String(build);
      const s = stampede(rate, build, expires, coalesce);
      const over = s.peak > DB_CAPACITY;
      q('[data-peak]').textContent = `${fmt(s.peak)} per second`;
      q('[data-peaknote]').textContent = `capacity ${fmt(DB_CAPACITY)}, including ${BASE_LOAD} from the rest of the site`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-peakbox]').style.setProperty('--c', over ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--role-1)');
      q('[data-extra]').textContent = fmt(s.extra);
      q('[data-extranote]').textContent = !expires ? 'the key never expires, so every request is a hit' : coalesce ? 'one request rebuilds it, the rest wait for that answer' : `${fmt(rate)} per second for ${build} s, one query per request`;
      const scale = Math.max(DB_CAPACITY, s.peak) * 1.1;
      const cols = q('[data-cols]'); cols.textContent = '';
      s.per.forEach((v, i) => {
        const col = document.createElement('div'); col.className = 'ce-col' + (v > DB_CAPACITY ? ' over' : '');
        const plot = document.createElement('span'); plot.className = 'ce-plot';
        const bar = document.createElement('span'); bar.className = 'ce-bar'; bar.style.height = `${(100 * v) / scale}%`;
        const n = document.createElement('span'); n.className = 'ce-n'; n.textContent = fmt(v); n.style.bottom = `calc(${(100 * v) / scale}% + 1px)`;
        plot.append(bar, n);
        const l = document.createElement('span'); l.className = 'ce-l'; l.textContent = `s${i}`;
        col.append(plot, l); cols.append(col);
      });
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-cap]').style.setProperty('--frac', String(DB_CAPACITY / scale));
      q('[data-chart]').setAttribute('aria-label', `Database queries per second over ${SECONDS} seconds: ${s.per.map((v, i) => `second ${i} ${fmt(v)}`).join(', ')}. Capacity is ${fmt(DB_CAPACITY)}.`);
      const v = q('[data-sverdict]'); v.classList.toggle('bad', over);
      v.textContent = !expires ? `The key does not expire, so the database sees only the ${BASE_LOAD} queries per second from the rest of the site.`
        : over ? `Overloaded: ${fmt(s.peak)} queries per second against a capacity of ${fmt(DB_CAPACITY)}. ${fmt(s.extra)} identical queries were sent to rebuild one value. A slow database makes the rebuild longer, which lets more requests miss.`
        : coalesce ? `Coalesced: ${fmt(s.extra)} query rebuilds the key, the peak is ${fmt(s.peak)} per second and the other requests wait about ${build} s for that answer.`
        : `Within capacity this time: peak ${fmt(s.peak)} per second, but ${fmt(s.extra)} identical queries were sent. A busier key or a slower rebuild would tip it over.`;
    }
    const schedule = () => { if (!frame) frame = requestAnimationFrame(draw); };
    ['[data-pattern]', '[data-policy]', '[data-size]', '[data-sr]', '[data-sb]', '[data-sx]', '[data-sc]'].forEach((sel) => { q(sel).addEventListener('input', schedule); q(sel).addEventListener('change', schedule); });
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-pattern]').value = DEFAULTS.pattern; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-policy]').value = DEFAULTS.policy; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-size]').value = DEFAULTS.size;
      schedule();
    });
    q('[data-sreset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-sr]').value = S_DEFAULTS.rate; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-sb]').value = S_DEFAULTS.build;
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-sx]').checked = S_DEFAULTS.expires; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-sc]').checked = S_DEFAULTS.coalesce;
      schedule();
    });
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .ce-h { margin: 8px 0 0; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .playground .ce-table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; max-width: 420px; font-size: .9rem; }
  .playground .ce-table caption { text-align: left; padding-bottom: 4px; }
  .playground .ce-table th, .playground .ce-table td { text-align: left; padding: 4px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-weight: 400; }
  .playground .ce-table thead th { font-weight: 600; }
  .playground .ce-table tr.sel th, .playground .ce-table tr.sel td { font-weight: 700; background: var(--accent-soft); }
  .playground .ce-strip { margin: 0; }
  .playground .ce-check { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .ce-chart { --ce-plot: 150px; --ce-label: 18px; position: relative; padding-top: 14px; }
  .playground .ce-cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(10, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 2px; }
  .playground .ce-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-width: 0; text-align: center; }
  .playground .ce-plot { position: relative; display: block; height: var(--ce-plot); }
  .playground .ce-n { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; font: .62rem var(--font-mono); overflow: hidden; }
  .playground .ce-bar { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; background: var(--role-1); border-radius: 3px 3px 0 0; min-height: 1px; transition: height .3s; }
  .playground .ce-col.over .ce-bar { background: var(--bad); }
  .playground .ce-l { font: .7rem var(--font-mono); color: var(--muted); height: var(--ce-label); line-height: var(--ce-label); }
  .playground .ce-cap { --frac: .9; position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: calc(var(--ce-label) + var(--ce-plot) * var(--frac)); border-top: 2px dashed var(--text); height: 0; pointer-events: none; }
  .playground .ce-cap span { position: absolute; right: 0; top: -1.3em; font-size: .7rem; color: var(--muted); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .playground .ce-bar { transition: none; } }
</style>
